{"record": "turn", "turn": 3, "seconds": 2.986, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 9722}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 9722, "cache_read_input_tokens": 3753, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 316, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_015hSqsJUdHgvfGkyAA6UNZk", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "For 4τ, the GCE-preferred DM mass decreases as r is lowered from 1 down to about r ≈ 0.5, then turns and increases again at smaller r. The paper says this change of direction \"may be related\" to competing effects of the mediator boost (γ_φ = 1/r) and the finite τ mass. At fixed m_χ, the τ-energy range is widest at r = √(2 m_τ / m_χ). For m_χ ≃ 15 GeV this gives r ≃ 0.49, close to where the region turns toward larger masses. The paper calls this link qualitative.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
